import re,shutil

def revise(page,photo,assets,base):
    folder=base/'Battle report photo sorting/02 Necrons vs Tau - diagonal wall'
    for n,name in [(19,'35 - 451008443_1442160463160052_6762849198851961609_n.jpg'),(20,'36 - 450600852_834050315332849_5013441927950128188_n.jpg')]:
        shutil.copy2(folder/name,assets/f'photo-{n:02}.jpg')
    page=page.replace('<small>ENGAGEMENT</small>T’au versus Necrons','<small>FORMAT</small>Matched Play · T’au vs Necrons').replace('<small>BATTLEFIELD</small>Central platform &amp; diagonal wall','<small>MISSION</small>Awaken the Data Spirits').replace('<small>FINAL SCORE</small>Not recorded','<small>FINAL SCORE</small>Necrons 18 · T’au 8')
    page=page.replace('A photographic reconstruction. The original written report has not been recovered. The Necron victory is confirmed by the player’s recollection; the final score, mission name, exact turning points and individual attack results are not recorded. The sections below describe visible stages of the fighting, with campaign prose connecting them.','The recovered account identifies this as the player’s first Matched Play game: Awaken the Data Spirits, ending 18–8 to the Necrons. Its photo groups are labelled at the end of rounds one through four. The narrative follows those groups; individual attacks, initiative rolls and round-by-round scores were not recorded.')
    intro='''<section id="engagement"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">02 / THE ENGAGEMENT</p><h2>Four rounds at the listening post.</h2><p>A stronger opening for Ghost Talon gives way to an aggressive push after round two. The recovered photo sequence shows the fight tightening around the platform before the Necrons finish ahead.</p></div><div class="opening">'''+photo(2,'Setup: the T’au deployment on one side of the diagonal wall, with Necrons beyond the central platform.')+'''<div class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">SETUP / MATCHED PLAY</p><h3>Awaken the Data Spirits</h3><p>This is a different test from the first battle’s Loot and Salvage. The player’s recovered account calls Awaken the Data Spirits a difficult mission for stealth suits, but describes a much better start to this game.</p><p>The diagonal wall cuts through the board and meets the raised communications platform. Rocky positions anchor opposite corners, while the Vox tower offers a narrow elevated position beside the main structure.</p><p>Ghost Talon has chosen Recon and Infiltration Tac Ops. The Necron cards show a Security set. Both forces must make their objectives work around a fight that increasingly draws them onto the same roof.</p></div></div>'''+photo(3,'Setup from the opposite end of the battlefield, showing the Necron deployment and central installation.')+'''<nav class="turn-nav" aria-label="Rematch rounds"><a href="#round-1">01 / The opening</a><a href="#round-2">02 / Positions established</a><a href="#round-3">03 / The push</a><a href="#round-4">04 / The finish</a></nav>'''
    rounds=[
    (1,'The better opening',6,'End of round one: T’au suits have reached the platform and approaches; Necrons occupy its opposite side.',[(8,'End of round one: stealth suits on the platform and flanks.'),(7,'End of round one: Necron infantry on the roof and around the platform.')],
    '<p>Ghost Talon makes contact with the installation. Two stealth suits occupy the near portion of the roof, while others remain on the approaches. Across the platform, Necron infantry establish their own positions.</p><p>The player remembered this opening as much better than the previous game. The end-of-round photographs show a T’au force actively contesting the structure, with suits still spread across the field rather than confined to one position.</p><p>The Necrons have also arrived in strength. The roof is already shared territory, with silver infantry at ground level beside the tower and rocky terrain.</p>'),
    (2,'Positions established',9,'End of round two: both forces are concentrated around the central platform, with T’au suits on the tower and rocky flank.',[(11,'End of round two: Necron infantry and T’au suits face one another around the array.'),(10,'End of round two: T’au hold the rocky rise and Vox tower while the platform remains contested.')],
    '<p>By the end of round two, the fight has several levels. A T’au suit occupies the Vox tower, another stands on a rocky rise, and both forces contest the raised installation.</p><p>The Necrons remain concentrated around the central array, with additional infantry covering the surrounding ground. Ghost Talon has positions from which to work, but fewer models with which to sustain the contest.</p><p>This is the point the player later identified as the hinge of the game: after round two, the T’au attack became too aggressive.</p>'),
    (3,'The push goes too far',15,'End of round three: the central fighting has tightened, with models down and surviving suits spread around the station.',[(14,'End of round three: a T’au suit beside the rocky terrain.'),(12,'End of round three: Necrons occupy the platform, with a model down beside a barricade.'),(13,'End of round three: a wider view of the Necron positions and the central stairs.')],
    '<p>Ghost Talon commits more aggressively after the second round. The account does not preserve each move or attack, but the player’s assessment is clear: the push allowed the Necrons to bring their greater number of models to bear.</p><p>The photographs at the end of round three show Necrons standing across the platform, a model fallen beside the approaches, and T’au suits operating around the outer positions.</p><p>In the Kappa-9 narrative, the advance has brought Ghost Talon close to the station’s systems. On the tabletop, the same commitment has left the cadre struggling against the Necron numbers.</p>'),
    (4,'The Necrons close it out',16,'End of round four: fallen models lie around the platform, while a T’au suit remains on the tower.',[(17,'End of round four: fallen T’au suits on the roof and a fallen Necron beside the steps.'),(18,'End of round four: Necrons remain on the platform and approaches; a T’au model lies down beside the wall.')],
    '<p>The final round leaves fallen models on the roof and beside the platform. Both sides have taken losses, but the Necrons retain a strong presence around the installation.</p><p>A stealth suit remains on the tower. Others are down near the wall and amid the central fighting. The photographs preserve the end positions, while the recovered account supplies the result: eighteen victory points for the Necrons, eight for the T’au.</p><p>The rematch breaks the first game’s deadlock. Ghost Talon began better, but the late aggression was punished, and T-601’s force takes the victory.</p>')]
    content=intro
    for n,title,main,caption,pairs,prose in rounds:
        cls='chapter reverse' if n%2==0 else 'chapter'
        content+=f'<div class="{cls}" id="round-{n}"><div class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">ROUND {n:02} / END-OF-ROUND RECORD</p><span class="chapter-no">{n:02}</span><h3>{title}</h3>{prose}</div>'+photo(main,caption)+'</div><div class="photo-pair landscape">'+''.join(photo(i,c) for i,c in pairs)+'</div>'
    content+='</section>'
    page=re.sub(r'<section id="engagement">.*?</section>',lambda _:content,page,count=1,flags=re.S)
    result='''<section id="results"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">03 / THE RESULT</p><h2>The dead claim the field.</h2><p>The recovered account confirms a decisive Necron win in the rematch.</p></div><div class="scoreboard" aria-label="Final result: T’au 8, Necrons 18, Necron victory"><div><small>T’AU / GHOST TALON</small><strong>8</strong><span>VICTORY POINTS</span></div><p>NECRON<br>VICTORY</p><div><small>NECRONS / T-601</small><strong>18</strong><span>VICTORY POINTS</span></div></div>
<div class="mvp-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">T’AU MVP / PLAYER’S PICK</p><h3>The suit by the wall</h3>'''+photo(19,'The player’s T’au MVP photograph: a stealth suit and Necron beside the wall.')+'''<p>The player singled out this stealth suit as their MVP. The surviving note does not give its individual kills or objective points, so those honours remain attached to the photographed operative without an invented tally.</p></div><div><p class="eyebrow">NECRON MVP / OPPONENT’S PICK</p><h3>The platform fight</h3>'''+photo(20,'The opponent’s MVP photograph: Necrons standing around a fallen stealth suit on the platform.')+'''<p>The opponent’s MVP is recorded in this close-up of the central fight. It places the recognition at the contested platform; the note does not specify the operative’s individual scoring or attack results.</p></div></div>
<details class="debrief" open><summary>From the tabletop · the player’s assessment</summary><div class="prose"><p>This was the player’s first Matched Play game, again using T’au. They felt they played much better at the beginning, while finding Awaken the Data Spirits a difficult mission for stealth suits.</p><p>The key mistake came after round two: the T’au became too aggressive, and the Necrons could overwhelm them with their greater number of models. The recorded final result is 18–8; no breakdown between mission points and Tac Ops survives in the supplied account.</p></div></details><div class="prose result-prose"><p>For the Kappa-9 campaign, T-601’s force has stopped Ghost Talon’s return. The result settles the engagement, while the fate of the listening post’s records remains part of the wider story.</p></div><a class="read" href="index.html">Revisit the first engagement <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>'''
    page=re.sub(r'<section id="results">.*?</section>',lambda _:result,page,count=1,flags=re.S)
    page=page.replace('Two sets of Tac Op cards appear in the photographs. They preserve the secondary objectives laid out for the game; the photographs do not establish which were achieved or how many points each scored.','The recovered message identifies Recon and Infiltration as the T’au choices: Vantage, Behind Enemy Lines and Triangulate. The opposing photographed set is Security: Central Control, Seize Ground and Hold the Line. Individual Tac Op scores were not recorded.')
    page=page.replace('Photographed Tac Ops: Vantage, Behind Enemy Lines and Triangulate.','T’au Tac Ops — Recon and Infiltration: Vantage, Behind Enemy Lines and Triangulate.').replace('Photographed Tac Ops: Central Control, Seize Ground and Hold the Line.','Necron Tac Ops — Security: Central Control, Seize Ground and Hold the Line.')
    page=re.sub(r'<div class="gallery">.*?</div></section>',lambda _:'<div class="gallery">'+photo(1,'An additional close-up of a T’au stealth suit on the Vox tower platform.')+'</div></section>',page,count=1,flags=re.S)
    page=page.replace('Based on the player’s rematch photographs and recollection of a Necron victory. Campaign framing continues Shadows over Kappa-9.','Based on the original battlefield photographs and the player’s recovered Facebook-thread account: first Matched Play game, Awaken the Data Spirits, Necrons 18–8. Round groupings and MVP selections follow that account. Campaign framing continues Shadows over Kappa-9.')
    page=page.replace('A photographic rematch report: Necron victory, reconstructed from the surviving battlefield photographs.','A Matched Play rematch on Awaken the Data Spirits: Necrons win 18–8. Four rounds, battlefield photographs and both MVP selections.')
    return page
